><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250522134951+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250522135806+10'00'" name="40159d32-ed2a-4399-bb81-84b5911c8106" page="0" coords="312.719000,219.949000,557.143000,219.949000,312.719000,210.154000,557.143000,210.154000,312.719000,209.518000,557.279000,209.518000,312.719000,199.722000,557.279000,199.722000,44.844500,199.028000,289.235000,199.028000,44.844500,189.233000,289.235000,189.233000,312.719000,199.030000,358.197000,199.030000,312.719000,189.234000,358.197000,189.234000,44.844500,188.597000,289.176000,188.597000,44.844500,178.801000,289.176000,178.801000,306.086000,188.598000,557.188000,188.598000,306.086000,178.644000,557.188000,178.803000,44.844500,178.109000,289.172000,178.109000,44.844500,168.313000,289.172000,168.313000,312.776000,178.110000,557.132000,178.110000,312.776000,168.315000,557.132000,168.315000,44.844500,167.677000,226.782000,167.677000,44.844500,157.882000,226.782000,157.882000,312.776000,167.679000,417.724000,167.679000,312.776000,157.884000,417.724000,157.884000,38.154300,157.189000,289.259000,157.189000,38.154300,147.235000,289.259000,147.394000,306.086000,157.191000,557.121000,157.191000,306.086000,147.236000,557.121000,147.396000,44.730500,146.758000,289.133000,146.758000,44.730500,136.963000,289.133000,136.963000,312.889000,146.760000,557.224000,146.760000,312.889000,136.964000,557.224000,136.964000,44.730500,136.270000,289.191000,136.270000,44.730500,126.475000,289.191000,126.475000,312.889000,136.272000,557.191000,136.272000,312.889000,126.476000,557.191000,126.476000,44.730500,125.839000,289.137000,125.839000,44.730500,116.043000,289.137000,116.043000,312.889000,125.840000,557.127000,125.840000,312.889000,116.045000,557.127000,116.045000,312.889000,115.352000,557.205000,115.352000,312.889000,105.557000,557.205000,105.557000,312.889000,104.921000,557.138000,104.921000,312.889000,94.798900,557.138000,95.125500,312.889000,94.432800,422.599000,94.432800,312.889000,84.637500,422.599000,84.637500" rect="37.848200,84.331400,557.586000,220.255000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>One in four academy athletes began their elite pathway with an injury,&#xD;with one in 10 athletes starting the season with a pre-existing&#xD;time-loss injury. Athletes entering the season with an injury had a&#xD;2.5 fold greater risk of subsequent in-season injury.&#xD;• Tertiary prevention strategies that involve both the management and&#xD;rehabilitation of a clinically diagnosed health problem, with ongoing&#xD;strategies to minimise the risk of subsequent injury should be a priority&#xD;for academy athletes starting their season with an injury. These&#xD;strategies should also be a priority for athletes below academy levels&#xD;(e.g. at community levels) who are striving to obtain future academy&#xD;scholarships.&#xD;• Injury characteristics, incidence, and burden differed between sport&#xD;programs. There was no gender specific risk difference in this cohort&#xD;across the scholarship period.&#xD;• Football, swimming, and the individual athlete program had the&#xD;highest physiotherapy to medical appointment ratios, while rowing&#xD;and rugby sevens had the lowest physiotherapy to medical appointment&#xD;ratios. Organisations with fixed or scarce resources should implement&#xD;health service delivery models to reflect the sport/program&#xD;specific requirements of clinical servicing from Physiotherapists and&#xD;Sports and Exercise Physicians.&#xD;&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>• One in four academy athletes began their elite pathway with an injury,&#xD;with one in 10 athletes starting the season with a pre-existing&#xD;time-loss injury. Athletes entering the season with an injury had a&#xD;2.5 fold greater risk of subsequent in-season injury.&#xD;• Tertiary prevention strategies that involve both the management and&#xD;rehabilitation of a clinically diagnosed health problem, with ongoing&#xD;strategies to minimise the risk of subsequent injury should be a priority&#xD;for academy athletes starting their season with an injury. These&#xD;strategies should also be a priority for athletes below academy levels&#xD;(e.g. at community levels) who are striving to obtain future academy&#xD;scholarships.&#xD;• Injury characteristics, incidence, and burden differed between sport&#xD;programs. There was no gender specific risk difference in this cohort&#xD;across the scholarship period.&#xD;• Football, swimming, and the individual athlete program had the&#xD;highest physiotherapy to medical appointment ratios, while rowing&#xD;and rugby sevens had the lowest physiotherapy to medical appointment&#xD;ratios. Organisations with fixed or scarce resources should implement&#xD;health service delivery models to reflect the sport/program&#xD;specific requirements of clinical servicing from Physiotherapists and&#xD;Sports and Exercise Physicians.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="0" rect="595.276000,127.949000,779.276000,219.949000"
/></highlight
